"id":"euler.lemma-2.3","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2.3","locator":"Lemma 2.3, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2.3.** Suppose that on $0\\le\\tau\\le T$ the entries of $B$ in the frame are $B_{12}=\\nu$, $B_{32}=\\eta$ and $B_{ij}=0$ otherwise, and that $E_c=0$. Then $\\sigma_p=\\sigma$, and the scaled components of the wave vector satisfy $$\\zeta_1'=-\\Bigl(1+\\frac1{2S^2}\\Bigr)\\zeta_2,\\qquad\n \\zeta_2'=-\\varepsilon\\zeta_3,\\qquad\n \\zeta_3'=\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2S^2}\\zeta_2 .$$ Where $\\zeta_3\\ne0$, the components $\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2$ of every amplitude vector satisfy $$\\begin{aligned}\n \\alpha_1'&=-\\alpha_2+\\zeta_1\\Pi,\\\\\n \\alpha_2'&=-\\Bigl(1-\\frac1{2S^2}\\Bigr)\\alpha_1\n   +\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2S^2}\\,\\frac{\\zeta_1\\alpha_1+\\zeta_2\\alpha_2}{\\zeta_3}\n   +\\frac{\\zeta_2}{S^2}\\,\\Pi,\n \\end{aligned}\n \\qquad\n \\Pi=\\frac{2\\zeta_2\\alpha_1+(\\zeta_1+\\varepsilon\\zeta_3)\\alpha_2}m .$$ As $S\\to\\infty$ with $\\varepsilon$ and $T$ fixed, $\\zeta\\to\\zeta_0$ uniformly on $[0,T]$, and the coefficients of this system for $(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)$ converge uniformly on $[0,T]$ to those of $$\\begin{equation}\n \\alpha_1'=-\\cos^2\\varphi(1-\\varepsilon\\tan\\varphi)\\alpha_2\n                 -\\varepsilon\\tau\\sin2\\varphi\\,\\alpha_1,\n \\qquad \\alpha_2'=-\\alpha_1 . \\tag{2.5}\n\\end{equation}$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/nodes/euler.lemma-2.3","id":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.3%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:db48fdd5ba2604749972848ed79e43c2768fdab18b46be5a44ed5375dec0afe1/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.3%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.2%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_cla